-- title:
--   Original fixed stopped-grid physical Taylor positive error vanishes in mean from Borel candidate jet
-- statement:
--   For actual bounded-variation X with Standing and original admissible D, on any deterministic physical grid with a stopped prefix endpoint at most T≤1, the true discounted original C1 Taylor error has integrable positive part and expected positive part converging to zero. Assume its samplewise compact C1 band and eventual small Y increment conditions; Lipschitz/derivative constants on the band; and Borel measurability of w and deriv w. The source-specific deterministic-grid theorem proves measurability of the actual X/D/J/Y finite Taylor sum, while the already Proved variable-endpoint BV mass DCT theorem proves integrability and expectation convergence. Thus no separate a.e. measurability assumption on Err is required, and no signed BV prebudget is used.
-- source:
--   Source-complete deterministic physical-grid adapter composing accepted 32541007 and new original deterministic error meas theorem. Supports original stopped-grid positive-error component of 2bc848f9.

